course: dictionary
lesson: 3264
title: Equipment: the things we need for a job
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Equipment is a noun for the tools, machines, clothes and other things you need for a job, sport or activity. The words around it give clues. «Put the equipment away» after a PE lesson tells you it means the balls, bats and cones you used.
explain: Equipment is uncountable, so we never say "an equipment" or "two equipments". To count it, say «a piece of equipment». In one sentence the writer puts «every fresh accoutrement» and then adds (piece of equipment) in brackets, which explains the hard word for you.
explain: Some equipment keeps you safe. Helmets, knee pads and life jackets are safety equipment. «Take off scarves, helmets and clothes with cords before playing on equipment, because they can catch and strangle.» The sentence warns you to take care on play equipment.
fact: Equipment means the tools, machines, clothes and other things you need for a job, sport or activity.
fact: Equipment is uncountable: say «a piece of equipment», not "an equipment".
fact: In science, equipment includes beakers, test tubes, thermometers and measuring cylinders, and you wear safety goggles when needed.
fact: In sport and PE, equipment includes balls, bats, cones and helmets, and safety equipment protects you.
fact: «Camping equipment» includes tents and sleeping bags, and «PE equipment» means the gear used in PE lessons.
exercise: «Never poke things into sockets, and keep away from substations, which are full of big electrical equipment.» What does equipment mean here? | Clothes you wear outdoors | *Machines and devices used for a job | Sleeping bags for camping | Food and drinks for a picnic
exercise: Which phrase is correct for one tool from a set? | two equipments | *a piece of equipment | an equipment | three equipment
exercise: «Take off scarves, helmets and clothes with cords before playing on equipment.» Which of these is safety equipment? | A football | A cone | A bat | *A helmet
test: «Looking up at the sky and breathing slowly is a simple calm practice that needs no special equipment.» What does this sentence suggest? | You need special gear to do it every day | *You do not need any tools or gear to do it | You must buy a telescope to do it
test: Which of these is camping equipment? | A test tube | A cone | *A tent | A bat
exam: «Blaming the referee, the equipment or a teammate after losing is a common habit.» What is this habit called? | A piece of context | *A self-serving bias | Camping equipment | Safety equipment
